! Westbrook & Dryer (1981) 2-Step Methane Combustion Mechanism
! Chemkin format for OpenFOAM chemkinReader
! Units: CAL/MOLE, MOLES, CM, S, K
! Reference: Combust. Sci. Technol., 27:31-43 (1981)

ELEMENTS
C  H  O  N
END

SPECIES
CH4  O2  CO  CO2  H2O  N2
END

REACTIONS  CAL/MOLE  MOLES
! Step 1: Methane partial oxidation (Table IV - High Temp, Ea = 48.4 kcal/mol)
! For low temp option (Ea = 30.0 kcal/mol), use A = 1.500E+07 and Ea = 30000.0
CH4 + 1.5 O2 => CO + 2 H2O                  6.700E+12   0.0   48400.0
FORD / CH4 0.2 /
FORD / O2 1.3 /

! Step 2f: Forward CO oxidation (Dryer & Glassman)
CO + 0.5 O2 + H2O => CO2 + H2O              3.981E+14   0.0   40000.0
FORD / CO 1.0 /
FORD / O2 0.25 /
FORD / H2O 0.5 /

! Step 2r: Reverse CO2 dissociation (Westbrook & Dryer 1981)
CO2 => CO + 0.5 O2                          5.000E+08   0.0   40000.0
FORD / CO2 1.0 /
END
